From: Peter M. <petermm@gmail.com>
Subject: [PATCH] Align ESP32-C6 modem clocks and PHY lifecycle with ESP-IDF

Use C6 LL clock dependencies, combined-radio calibration on first enable,
PLL tracking and RF shutdown. Preserve nested Wi-Fi/PHY/I2C interrupt state
in IRAM. C6 uses the non-retention wakeup path; backup DMA is C3-specific.

diff --git a/src/rtems_esp_wifi_init.c b/src/rtems_esp_wifi_init.c
--- a/src/rtems_esp_wifi_init.c
+++ b/src/rtems_esp_wifi_init.c
@@ -29,7 +29,7 @@
  * Read ESP-IDF's with power management, PSRAM, coexistence, MAC/BB power down,
  * NAN, the roaming app and tickless idle all off and nine calls are left.
  * Seven are in libnet80211.a.  This file is those seven in ESP-IDF's order,
- * plus the PHY lifecycle. C3/C5 calibration runs on first PHY enable, with
+ * plus the PHY lifecycle. C3/C5/C6 calibration runs on first PHY enable, with
  * wakeup and periodic tracking thereafter, matching esp_phy_enable().
  *
  * What this file does NOT do, so nobody looks for it here:
